{"id":"G1392","lemma":"δοξάζω","transliteration":"doxazō","sayIt":"doxazō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to glorify","meaning":"δοξάζω\n(δόξα), [in LXX chiefly for כָּבַד ni., pi., also for פָּאַר, etc. ;]\n1. to think, suppose, hold an opinion (Æsch., Plat., al.).\n2. To bestow δόξα (which see) on, to magnify, extol, praise (Thuc., iii, 45; Plut., al.): with accusative, Mat.5:16, Mrk.2:12, Jhn.8:54, Rom.15:6, 1Pe.2:12, al.; id. before ἐπί Luk.2:20; ἐν, Gal.1:24, 1Pe.4:16.\n3. In LXX and NT (see: δόξα, 3), to clothe with splendour, glorify (Exo.34:29-30, Psa.37:20, Isa.44:23, Est.3:1, al): Rom.8:30, 2Co.3:10, 2Th.3:1, 1Pe.1:8, al.; of Christ, Jhn.7:39 8:54, al. (on the Johannine use, see Cremer, 211; Westc., Jo., Intr.); of the Father, Jhn.13:31-32, 1Pe.4:11, al. (cf. ἐν-, συν-δοξάζω).\n(AS)","glosses":["glorified","glorify","glorifying","honored","may be glorified","has glorified"],"count":53,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorify","kjv":"glorify"}},{"chapterId":"mat-6","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"be honored","kjv":"they may have glory"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorified","kjv":"glorified"}},{"chapterId":"mat-15","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"they glorified","kjv":"they glorified"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-2","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorified","kjv":"glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-2","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorifying","kjv":"glorifying"}},{"chapterId":"luk-4","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"and was glorified","kjv":"being glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-5","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorifying","kjv":"glorifying"}},{"chapterId":"luk-5","v":26,"renderings":{"bsb":"glorified","kjv":"they glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-7","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"they glorified","kjv":"they glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-13","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"began to glorify","kjv":"glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-17","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"praising","kjv":"glorified"}},{"chapterId":"luk-18","v":43,"renderings"