,"source":"web"},{"ref":"John 7:39","note":"But he said this about the Spirit, which those believing in him were to receive. For the Holy Spirit was not yet given, because Jesus wasn’t yet glorified.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 3:13","note":"The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified his Servant Jesus, whom you delivered up, and denied in the presence of Pilate…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 1:21","note":"Because knowing God, they didn’t glorify him as God, and didn’t give thanks, but became vain in their reasoning, and their senseless heart was darkened.","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20","note":"for you were bought with a price. Therefore glorify God in your body and in your spirit, which are God’s.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 3:10","note":"For most certainly that which has been made glorious has not been made glorious in this respect, by reason of the glory that surpasses.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G1722","lemma":"ἐν","transliteration":"en","gloss":"in/on/among"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}